    <statement><p>Find the vector parameterization for the line which passes through the origin and is perpendicular to the xz-plane.</p>
<p><var form="buttons">
<li>
<p><m>\left\lt t,0,0\right&gt;</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lt t,0,t\right&gt;</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lt 0,0,t\right&gt;</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\left\lt 0,t,0\right&gt;</m></p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
    <solution><m>v(t) = P + t*\mathbf{w}</m>



Since the line passes through the origin, P = 0.



<m>\mathbf{w}</m> can be any vector of the form <m>\left\lt 0,C,0\right&gt;</m> with <m>C \neq 0</m>.



The only answer that matches these is <m>\left\lt 0,t,0\right&gt;</m>.


</solution>
